**Read:** [Perple_X — Connolly, phase-equilibrium methods and examples](../sources/Perple-X-Methods-and-Documentation.lingua#r_39E8B7CK16VF55MXWKSXMNN4Z6), the complete introductory tutorial, strategy/limitations, data compatibility, and benchmark discussions; [HPx-eos and THERMOCALC — models, data, and interpretation](../sources/HPx-eos-and-THERMOCALC.lingua#r_0QYHHGNWRA8RQEM5MADWXDRQFJ), the full relevant model/data explanation and original papers; [MAGEMin, an efficient Gibbs energy minimizer — Riel and colleagues](../sources/MAGEMin-Riel-2022.lingua#r_7JK9DVER7XW4ESPJ27K7H9K29S), the complete article, tests, and relevant supplement.

A phase-equilibrium result depends on thermodynamic datasets, reference states, solution models, selected phases/components, constraints, and numerical settings. Record each version and its calibration range. A familiar software name does not establish that any mixture of downloaded data and models is internally consistent.

Compare minimization/grid strategies, endmember treatment, convergence, phase suppression, and refinement with documented benchmarks. Different program outputs can disagree because of numerical strategy or because they solved different thermodynamic problems. Matching colors or mineral abbreviations is not a controlled comparison.

The Perple_X documentation identifies outdated material and specific dataset/model incompatibilities. The HPx-eos authors explain their models and intended uses; the MAGEMin paper develops/tests an algorithm. Read their complete relevant methods to distinguish implementation behavior from the experimental evidence or geological assumptions underlying a model.

**Work:** reproduce an authorized benchmark with all inputs/versions/settings explicit in your study workspace. Independently check mass balance, nonnegative amounts, limiting cases, and at least one phase relation. Change numerical resolution separately from model/data choices and explain the different effects. Test against a geological observation not used to tune the calculation.

Read complete papers and tutorials rather than interpreting a default output as a measurement. Continue through [Explain igneous materials through melting, crystallization, and field relations](../../geology/materials/Melting-crystallization-and-igneous-bodies.lingua#r_7QWRZH8D2EVJR6F20Z77Y4QXR7) for the shared melting/crystallization foundation before the deeper magma and igneous-process sequence.

**Continue:** [Explain igneous materials through melting, crystallization, and field relations](../../geology/materials/Melting-crystallization-and-igneous-bodies.lingua#r_7QWRZH8D2EVJR6F20Z77Y4QXR7).

**Return:** [Mineralogy and petrology — minerals, crystals, rock processes, and investigation](../Mineralogy-and-petrology.lingua#r_44F7X6GPMW6ZSCCN6D71QSVKBN).
